# explore-sector survey config -- copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env   &&   $EDITOR .env
#
# `explore-live.sh` sources `.env` from this folder (set -a), then runs the
# survey against an ALREADY-RUNNING live client sitting at character-select --
# it does NOT start our docker stack and never launches the client itself.
#
# Only the values that actually vary per machine live here. Every coordinate /
# threshold knob the scripts read has a baked-in default and is NOT listed --
# override one only if the HUD layout changed (see SKILL.md "First-run
# calibration"). Do not paste server IPs or the repo path in here.

# ---- REQUIRED -------------------------------------------------------------

# The character to enter from the character-select screen. OCR locates this
# name in the top-left quadrant, so it must match what the client renders.
ENB_EXPLORE_CHARACTER_NAME=YourCharacter

# Where a whole survey lives: per-sector ledgers (<Sector>.json), actions.log,
# and captures/. Point it OUTSIDE the repo so progress + pcaps are not in git.
# Re-using the same path RESUMES a survey (completed sectors are skipped).
ENB_EXPLORE_WORKDIR=/absolute/path/to/your/survey-workdir

# ---- LIVE-MODE DEFAULTS (explore-live.sh forces/sets these; override if needed) ----

# 1 = you own the client + proxy; the survey never kills/relaunches them.
# explore-live.sh forces this on -- listed here only for visibility.
ENB_EXPLORE_MANUAL_CLIENT=1

# Capture the real WINE proxy (host process, exact `comm` name) instead of the
# dockerized FreyaProxy. This is what a live client connects through.
ENB_EXPLORE_PROXY_NAME=Net7Proxy.exe

# 1 = start the per-sector packet capture at char-select (the entry handshake),
# then one file per sector. Needs the capture worker installed once:
#   sudo bash scripts/pcap-install.sh
ENB_PCAP=1

# ---- OPTIONAL TUNING ------------------------------------------------------

# Unattended deadman: if this many SECONDS pass with no nav visited/skipped,
# drive.py kills the client and STOPS the run. Empty/0 = disabled.
ENB_EXPLORE_KILL_NO_PROGRESS=1800

# Hard cap on sectors driven in one survey run, and how many consecutive
# already-complete arrivals end it (the reachable graph is exhausted).
# ENB_SURVEY_MAX=90
# ENB_SURVEY_STALE_MAX=3

# X display the WINE client renders on (defaults to :0).
# DISPLAY=:0
